{
  "dom_id": "step-q97661",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $70$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store does not have the first $10$ issues in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the expected value of the chosen issue?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number of the selected issue. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{11,12…,70\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{11,12,…,70\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11+70}{2}=40.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen number is $40.5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
